  "about": "docs/testing.md's results table is generated from this file by scripts/test-results.py. Edit a test's description under tests; results (the newest per test and mode) are written by the script from compat.yml's result artifacts. Seeded 2026-11-04 from the hand table: pull request run 41768213339 (every test that isn't large) and run 41770338111 on main (GitLab and GitLab Runner).",
  "tests": [
    {
      "test": "vault-2",
      "runs": "Vault **2.2.1** (`bigbang-vault`)",
      "notes": "Big Bang pins 1.21. A fresh install; vault-upgrade covers existing data. Check: `vault status` initialized and unsealed; a KV v2 secret written and read back"
    },
    {
      "test": "release-upgrade",
      "runs": "Kyverno (Enforce), Headlamp and Grafana installed from the newest release (`<Big Bang>-cg.<n>`), then upgraded to the change's Flux and overlays. On 4.0 the newest release was `3.35.1-cg.62`, so the test crosses the major: Big Bang 3's keys and ClusterPolicies first, then Big Bang 4's `packages.*` and CEL policies",
      "notes": "What a site pinned to a release does when it moves to the next one. Check: Kyverno admits the org image and refuses docker.io before and after; Grafana's database ok; no pod still runs an image digest the release pinned and the change replaced"
    },
    {
      "test": "vault-upgrade",
      "runs": "Iron Bank's Vault 1.21 with a KV secret, upgraded to `bigbang-vault` 2.x; the secret read back",
      "notes": "Needs an Iron Bank login (`registry1: true`): **SKIPPED** in CI until the `REGISTRY1_USERNAME` and `REGISTRY1_PASSWORD` secrets exist"
    },
    {
      "test": "sonarqube-26.10",
      "runs": "SonarQube **26.10** community with its JMX exporter init container (`bigbang-jmx-exporter`, built and loaded by the test)",
      "notes": "Big Bang pins 26.9 and turns the exporter on only with monitoring; the test turns it on and checks the javaagent serves JVM metrics"
    },
    {
      "test": "alloy",
      "runs": "grafana-alloy 1.21, config-reloader 0.94",
